Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["1D-MATH-EXPECTATION", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.996335738629848*^9, 3.9963357454370737`*^9}, 
   3.996672469810019*^9, {3.996753015752389*^9, 3.996753019402701*^9}, 
   3.996753740817995*^9, {3.997449762190651*^9, 3.997449762656846*^9}, {
   3.997459146152009*^9, 3.997459148686284*^9}, 3.9974604855823*^9, {
   3.9974764216017237`*^9, 
   3.9974764219466352`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"99a53d45-81f6-4a19-b28b-\
73c3b0f58e23"],

Cell["\<\
The 1D-MATH-EXPECTATION test suite rigorously verifies that the analytical \
functions responsible for evaluating position, momentum, force, and energy \
expectation values are mathematically exact. It accomplishes this by \
systematically comparing the explicitly coded expectation functions against \
continuous integration performed over a robust symbolic parameter bus. To \
ensure the stable evaluation of these complex integrals by the computer \
algebra system without encountering zero-variance singularities, this \
specific suite employs purely real-valued position and momentum input \
parameters. Leveraging the previously established wavefunction and density \
constructs alongside GWP1DASSUMPTIONS, the tests successfully validate \
advanced quantum mechanical operators, confirming the accuracy of \
kinetic-potential cross-terms, phase-space covariance, and the complete \
hydrodynamic decomposition of the system\[CloseCurlyQuote]s total energy.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.9967562053117743`*^9, 3.9967568537392187`*^9, {3.9974615497369013`*^9, 
   3.997461554417214*^9}, {3.997461769845903*^9, 3.997461777601955*^9}, {
   4.000410447889563*^9, 
   4.000410448659226*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"f11c3c82-64d9-4269-ae9f-\
9a0f74f34814"],

